<title>CANADA: Imperial Oil raises posted oil prices.</title>
<headline>Imperial Oil raises posted oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Oil Ltd said it raised the price it would pay for some grades of crude oil by C$6.00/cubic metre or C$0.95/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The new prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Edmonton light sweet C$187.00/cubic metre, or C$29.73/barrel</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$182.00/cubic metre, or C$28.94/barrel</p>
<p>Bow River at Hardisty C$163.00/cubic metre, or C$25.91/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$171.00/cubic metre, or C$27.19/barrel</p>
<p>-- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
</text>
